    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0530" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51/839: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washburn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-20T10:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                                1927—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 20—8:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>54. The Chancellor has officially and urgently requested me to report that he
                    would appreciate very much an early reply to the question on pages 3 and
                        4<anchor n="6" xml:id="d322-f1"/> of my despatch No. 1508 of August 30th.
                    The reasons for the urgency of the request are connected with the meeting of the
                    Austrian Control Committee in London on October 11th. Further details are given
                    in my despatch of this date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d322-f1" n="6" xml:id="d322-f1-content">
                <p>The 3d and 5th paragraphs of the preceding despatch.</p>
